# Security response headers, applied by Cloudflare Pages to every response.
# Ported from satrio.io's baseline (C:\SatrioTsubasa\GitHub\satrio.io\public\_headers) and adjusted
# for this repo: a static, self-contained docs app with no CMS, no forms, and no third-party
# scripts/beacons — so satrio.io's Cloudflare Web Analytics allowances (script-src
# static.cloudflareinsights.com, connect-src cloudflareinsights.com) are dropped rather than ported,
# and img-src drops satrio.io's "https:" (this app never loads a remote image). satrio.io's
# "media-src 'self' https:" is dropped entirely (no media-src directive here): this app ships no
# audio/video anywhere, so the stricter default-src 'self' fallback governs it instead.
#
# script-src carries a sha256 hash instead of plain 'self': index.html ships one inline <script>
# (the pre-paint theme stamp — mirrors src/docs/ThemeControl.tsx's applyDocsTheme mapping so <html>
# is themed before first paint, see index.html's own comment) that 'self' alone would block, and a
# nonce isn't available to a prerendered static file with no server-side templating. The hash below
# is exact-content: it MUST be regenerated (sha256, base64) whenever that inline script's text
# changes, or the browser will silently drop the CSP-violating script (no build error — the console
# shows a CSP violation and the pre-paint theme stamp stops running).
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-Cl+E3bN1J/9XAbjopm3HCRxsDHISmmNk+KLWTZfrWRE='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), browsing-topics=()
